# System architecture

Modular Next.js monolith. Business logic lives in `modules/<domain>/`. UI never queries Prisma.

## Folders

```
app/(auth)/                 login, register, forgot-password
app/(dashboard)/            dashboard, leads, clients, projects, bidding, …
app/(portal)/               client + freelancer portals (role-gated)
app/api/graphql/            GraphQL Yoga
app/api/stripe/             webhook (raw body + signature)
app/api/cron/               expire-bids, expire-proposals, overdue invoices, reminders
components/ui/              shadcn primitives
components/{layout,tables,forms,modals,charts}/
components/{bidding,projects,invoices}/   domain-specific UI only
lib/{auth,graphql,prisma,permissions,tenant,validation,storage,email,stripe,notifications,audit,errors}/
modules/<domain>/           service.ts, validation.ts, schema.ts, resolvers.ts
prisma/schema.prisma        prisma/seed.ts
tests/                      unit/integration for critical workflows
proxy.ts                    auth/session gate (not middleware.ts)
```

Domain modules: `auth`, `organizations`, `users`, `roles`, `leads`, `clients`, `opportunities`, `proposals`, `projects`, `bidding`, `resources`, `contracts`, `milestones`, `tasks`, `time-tracking`, `invoices`, `payments`, `expenses`, `notifications`, `files`, `reports`, `audit`.

## GraphQL merge

Each module exports schema + resolvers. `lib/graphql` merges them into Yoga. Pages talk to GraphQL (or a thin server action that calls the **same** service). Never duplicate rules in the UI.

## Tenant scoping

Every org-owned entity has `organizationId`. Derive it from the authenticated membership session — never from client input.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
prisma.project.findUnique({ where: { id: projectId } })

// ✅ GOOD
prisma.project.findFirst({
  where: { id: projectId, organizationId: ctx.organizationId },
})
```

Reuse this pattern for update/delete. Composite unique keys that include `organizationId` where it prevents cross-tenant collisions (e.g. invoice numbers).
